# Architecture

Strict layered architecture with clear dependency boundaries.

```
Page / API route  →  Service  →  Repository  →  Mongoose Model
                         ↓
                    Serializer (DTO shaping)
```

## Layer rules

- **Pages & API routes** — orchestration only. No business logic, no direct Mongoose calls.
- **Services** (`src/lib/services/*.service.ts`) — business logic, authorization, transactions, domain rules.
- **Repositories** (`src/lib/repositories/*.repository.ts`) — persistence only. No cross-domain business rules.
- **Serializers** (`src/lib/serializers/`) — shape DTOs for the UI. Reuse across pages and APIs.
- **Validators** (`src/lib/validators/`) — Zod schemas. Parse in API routes and services.

## Export pattern

Services and repositories export **plain objects**, not classes:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export const beatService = { async create(...) { ... } };

// ❌ BAD — no classes
export class BeatService { ... }
```

## Feature-first organization

```
src/features/beats/       — beat-pack UI types, shared beat logic
src/features/payments/    — payment-related shared code
src/features/studio/      — producer dashboard components
src/components/ui/        — generic UI primitives (shadcn)
src/components/layout/    — app shell components
src/components/           — shared app-level components
```

## Dependency boundaries

- Pages → services (never repositories or models directly)
- Services → repositories (never models directly when a repository exists)
- Repositories → models + `connectDB()`
- Components → never import services or repositories
- Feature code stays within its feature boundary
